# <type>(<scope>): <subject>   ── ≤ 50 chars, imperative mood, no trailing period
#
# ── Body ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Explain WHAT changed and WHY (not how). Wrap at 72 chars. Blank line above.
#
#
# ── Footer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks and the migration path>
# Closes #<issue>   |   Refs #<issue>
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits — https://www.conventionalcommits.org
#
#   type   = feat | fix | docs | style | refactor | perf | test | build | ci
#            | chore | revert
#   scope  = optional area, e.g. editor, preview, export, docker, ci, deps
#
# Examples:
#   feat(export): add JPEG quality slider
#   fix(preview): stop drag from selecting SVG text
#   docs(readme): document the run/stop commands
#   ci(release): publish GitHub release on tag push
#
# A `feat` bumps the MINOR version, `fix` bumps PATCH, and a `BREAKING CHANGE`
# footer (or `type!:`) bumps MAJOR. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
